The major product $\mathbf{Y}$ in the following reaction scheme is:
Pyridine $\xrightarrow{\text{(i) } \text{HBr};\; \text{(ii) } \text{Br}_2} \mathbf{X}$ [an organic salt];
*trans*-stilbene ($\text{Ph–CH}=\text{CH–Ph}$) $\xrightarrow{\mathbf{X},\; \text{AcOH}} \mathbf{Y}$.

Correct statement(s) about $\mathbf{Q}$ and $\mathbf{R}$ is/are:
*trans*-1,2-dimethylcyclohexane-1,2-diol $\xrightarrow{\text{H}_3\text{O}^+} \mathbf{Q}$;
*cis*-1,2-dimethylcyclohexane-1,2-diol $\xrightarrow{\text{H}_3\text{O}^+} \mathbf{R}$.
